I'm so sorry for never posting the final version when I said I would. Like 
most of the projects I attempt, I got stuck with this one at a late stage 
and became distracted with new ideas. The system is now finished, and I'd 
love to answer some of the questions from this thread (which I found just 
now by googling random lojban things).

- The final version is now "Version 4". Any material you see pertaining to 
earlier versions is out of date.
- The finished PDF was released a month or so ago and is online here: public 
Google Docs<https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B0aL1oAS_j4yZjZKa3ZYYUNUdnVZdHdEMW5pMGdJUQ/edit?pli=1#>
- The graphics in the examples were rendered using the Opentype font that I 
developed along with the orthography. All the glyphs are complete, but 
unfortunately I was unable to complete the Opentype scripting required to 
make the font usable (this where I got stuck and gave up in 2010). The 
system has custom glyph combination rules and the Opentype system was too 
difficult for me to create such a complex system. I am convinced it can be 
done though, so if you know anyone who is skilled with font creation then 
I'd love to collaborate to release a finished font. If you'd like the 
unfinished font to create graphics from the glyphs, I'd be happy to supply 
it.
- The font (and the vectors for individual glyphs) was created with a 
combination of FontLab and FontForge.

Sorry if I'm gravedigging by replying to this. I put a lot of effort and 
cared a great deal about this project so it's very exciting when someone is 
interested.

ki'e
mu'o

